D. Possible project direction:
I would investigate these six directions.
Research direction	What you investigate
1. Urban feature extraction	Accurate identification of buildings, roads, vegetation and open spaces
2. Public-space assessment	Distribution, coverage and accessibility of parks and open spaces
3. Urban growth monitoring	Changes in built-up areas, vegetation and infrastructure over time
4. Road-network intelligence	Road connectivity, missing links and spatial distribution
5. Indian urban morphology	Performance of existing AI models in dense, heterogeneous Indian cities
6. Multi-source data fusion	Combining optical, SAR, GIS and other geographical datasets

GeoAI-Based Urban Spatial Intelligence for Public-Space and Infrastructure Planning
An integrated framework for extracting urban features from satellite imagery, quantifying their spatial characteristics and assessing the distribution and accessibility of public spaces in selected Indian urban areas.

Core research questions:
1. How accurately can computer vision extract urban features from satellite imagery?
2. Can these extracted features be converted into reliable urban-planning indicators?
3. Can geospatial analysis identify neighbourhoods with relatively poor access to public green spaces?
4. How well do existing models perform in different types of Indian urban environments?

